  "scope": "Full new attachment, the two preceding screenshots and the accumulated cutoff/echo/source-generator work. Paper derivations only; no new Lean declaration, compiler run or CI claim.",
  "claims_checked": {
    "cut_inverse": "Exact mixed cutoff/cut differences recover every edge at fixed time. The full ambient inverse edge cost is sqrt(m)*(Y-k), with m<=4; the complete total instead costs sqrt(Y-1). Source-restricted optimal cost is not identified with the arbitrary-edge cost.",
    "kernel_convolution": "C=g*nu is an exact finite signed convolution. Using only the public bounded remainder and its early branch, employ g_c(t)=exp(-c*t)g(t), 0<c<1, and nu_c with each impulse weight multiplied by (ab)^(-c). Then g_c belongs to L1 and L2 and C_c=g_c*nu_c has an ordinary Fourier factorization. Unweighted Fourier statements require an independently paid ordinary transform domain or tempered distributions. Fourier division is not used in the cut inverse.",
