    "arithmetic_coefficients": "The same self-echo equals sum_(n>=4) (Lambda*Lambda)(n)/sqrt(n) (H*H)(L-log n). Dirichlet associativity yields Lambda*Lambda=(mu*mu)*(log*log), with all ordered multiplicities and prime powers retained.",
    "operator_domain": "The proved ||A_epsilon||<605/621 supplies a Neumann inverse for I-A_epsilon, not for A_epsilon. The original equation is A_epsilon X=Y after actual L2 membership has been established. For H=q*j, the exact forcing changes from Y_j to q*Y_j; compact smoothing is not inverted without a bound.",
    "RH_strength": "The all-positive-rate eventual absolute bound for P*P is DERIVED equivalent to RH for this exact fixed source. Initial Laplace identity holds on Re z>1/2. A right off-line zero of any multiplicity m yields a double pole with nonzero leading coefficient m^2*K_H(rho-1/2)^2. Under RH the full absolutely summable zero family and bounded Arch term bound P, giving P*P=O(L). The all-rate bound is not proved here."
